              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">9a4b2d88-6386-4ba0-9994-0cd54b139222</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Description</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Purpose: How open the view is from points on a surface, and how much of a target each point can see.
Fidelity: Screening - geometric ray casting; a plan-view measure, not a daylight metric.
Method: Viewshed casts a 26 degree half-angle cone out to 48 m from each mesh vertex; View Target casts rays to the target past shared context.
Result: Values from 0 to 1, with colours, per observer point.
Needs: Nothing to install; runs inside Rhino. Runtime: seconds to minutes.
Edit: Context, observer surfaces and target; wire normals to aim the cones.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
